    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nElectronic structure of sodium nitroprusside.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nNa2[Fe(CN)5(NO)] where NO is nitrosonium ligand (NO+).\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\n2(+1) + x + 5(-1) + (+1) = 0 => x - 2 = 0 => x = +2.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. In sodium nitroprusside, the nitric oxide ligand is present as nitrosonium ion NO+.\n2. Cyanide CN- is -1 each.\n3. Sum: 2(+1) + x + 5(-1) + 1 = 0 => x = +2.\n4. Thus, iron is in the +2 oxidation state (low spin d6, diamagnetic).\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: +2\n\n6. WHY OTHER OPTIONS ARE WRONG:\nOlder literature assumed NO was neutral giving Fe(III), but magnetic and spectroscopic measurements confirm diamagnetic Fe(II) and NO+.",
