    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nNon-stoichiometric defect calculations in wustite.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nFormula: Fe0.93O contains Fe2+ and Fe3+ ions balancing one O2- ion.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nLet fraction of Fe3+ be y. Then fraction of Fe2+ is (0.93 - y). Equation: 2(0.93 - y) + 3y = 2.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. 1.86 - 2y + 3y = 2 => y = 2 - 1.86 = 0.14.\n2. Percentage of Fe(III) = (0.14 / 0.93) x 100% = 15.05% ~ 15%.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 15%\n\n6. WHY OTHER OPTIONS ARE WRONG:\nThe remaining 85% of iron ions exist as Fe(II).",
