    "id": "redox-mcq-436",
    "questionNumber": 436,
    "question": "Calculated analytical problem: When 1 mole of Sn2+ is oxidized to Sn4+ by acidic K2Cr2O7, how many moles of Cr2O7(2-) are consumed?",
    "options": {
      "A": "1/3 mole",
      "B": "3 moles",
      "C": "1/2 mole",
      "D": "1/6 mole"
    },
    "optionsList": [
      "1/3 mole",
      "3 moles",
      "1/2 mole",
      "1/6 mole"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nStoichiometry of dichromate with tin(II).\n\n2. GIVEN:\nCr2O7(2-) + 3Sn2+ + 14H+ -> 2Cr3+ + 3Sn4+ + 7H2O.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nMole ratio: 1 mole Cr2O7(2-) oxidizes 3 moles Sn2+.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Each Sn2+ loses 2 electrons (Sn2+ -> Sn4+).\n2. 1 mole of Cr2O7(2-) accepts 6 electrons.\n3. Therefore, 1 mole of Cr2O7(2-) reacts with 6/2 = 3 moles of Sn2+.\n4. Hence, 1 mole of Sn2+ requires 1/3 mole of Cr2O7(2-).\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 1/3 mole\n\n6. WHY OTHER OPTIONS ARE WRONG:\nSince 3 Sn2+ require 1 Cr2O7(2-), 1 Sn2+ requires 1/3 Cr2O7(2-).",
    "solutionStructured": {
      "concept": "Stoichiometry of dichromate with tin(II).",
      "given": "Cr2O7(2-) + 3Sn2+ + 14H+ -> 2Cr3+ + 3Sn4+ + 7H2O.",
      "formula": "Mole ratio: 1 mole Cr2O7(2-) oxidizes 3 moles Sn2+.",
      "stepByStep": "1. Each Sn2+ loses 2 electrons (Sn2+ -> Sn4+).\n2. 1 mole of Cr2O7(2-) accepts 6 electrons.\n3. Therefore, 1 mole of Cr2O7(2-) reacts with 6/2 = 3 moles of Sn2+.\n4. Hence, 1 mole of Sn2+ requires 1/3 mole of Cr2O7(2-).",
      "finalAnswer": "Option A: 1/3 mole",
      "whyOtherOptionsWrong": "Since 3 Sn2+ require 1 Cr2O7(2-), 1 Sn2+ requires 1/3 Cr2O7(2-)."
    },
